'''''Glaucium corniculatum''''', the '''blackspot hornpoppy'''<ref>{{PLANTS|id=GLCL3|taxon=Glaucium corniculatum|accessdate=19 January 2016}}</ref> or '''red horned-poppy''',<ref name=BSBI07>{{BSBI 2007 |accessdate=2014-10-17 }}</ref> is a species of the genus ''[[Glaucium]]'' in the poppy family ([[Papaveraceae]]). It is an annual [[flowering plant]], occurring in southern Europe, and grows up to 1 foot (30&nbsp;cm) high. The stem and leaves are hairy, the capsule fruit is covered with stiff hair, the flower is red, with a black spot on the base of the tepal bract, which has a yellow margin around it. The flower appears from June until August.

